WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.417
Welcome to UFI Career Studio. Build a resume

00:00:03.417 --> 00:00:06.834
for the role. Turn the job description into

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:10.251
a focused resume that makes your strongest evidence

00:00:10.251 --> 00:00:13.668
easy to find. We will work through five

00:00:13.668 --> 00:00:17.085
practical steps, with examples you can adapt to

00:00:17.085 --> 00:00:18.366
your own experience.

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:22.736
Begin with one job description, not every job

00:00:22.736 --> 00:00:26.306
you might apply for. Highlight three responsibilities and

00:00:26.306 --> 00:00:29.875
the skills mentioned more than once. For a

00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:33.445
support role, these might be resolving customer issues,

00:00:33.445 --> 00:00:37.014
documenting solutions, and working across teams. Keep this

00:00:37.014 --> 00:00:40.584
short list next to your resume. It gives

00:00:40.584 --> 00:00:44.153
you a practical way to decide what deserves

00:00:44.153 --> 00:00:45.492
the most space.

00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:50.323
For each priority, choose something you have actually

00:00:50.323 --> 00:00:54.313
done that demonstrates it. Evidence can come from

00:00:54.313 --> 00:00:58.303
paid work, school, volunteering, or a personal project.

00:00:58.303 --> 00:01:02.293
If the employer needs coordination, describe how you

00:01:02.293 --> 00:01:06.283
organized people or deadlines. Do not copy requirements

00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:10.273
you cannot support. A smaller set of relevant,

00:01:10.273 --> 00:01:14.263
honest examples is stronger than a long list

00:01:14.263 --> 00:01:16.258
of impressive sounding claims.

00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:20.671
Replace a responsibility with an action and a

00:01:20.671 --> 00:01:24.258
result. Instead of saying responsible for reports, explain

00:01:24.258 --> 00:01:27.846
that you rebuilt a weekly reporting process and

00:01:27.846 --> 00:01:31.433
reduced preparation time. Use a number only when

00:01:31.433 --> 00:01:35.021
you can explain where it came from. If

00:01:35.021 --> 00:01:38.608
you do not have a metric, describe the

00:01:38.608 --> 00:01:42.196
visible improvement, such as clearer handoffs, fewer repeated

00:01:42.196 --> 00:01:44.438
questions, or a completed launch.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.728
Make the document easy for a person to

00:01:48.728 --> 00:01:52.206
read before worrying about a score. Use familiar

00:01:52.206 --> 00:01:55.684
headings such as Experience, Education, and Skills. Keep

00:01:55.684 --> 00:01:59.162
dates consistent and avoid putting essential information inside

00:01:59.162 --> 00:02:02.640
decorative graphics. After exporting, check that you can

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.118
select and copy the text. Then open the

00:02:06.118 --> 00:02:09.596
file on another screen to make sure the

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:12.640
spacing and page breaks still look intentional.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.965
Now practice a ten second review. Look away,

00:02:16.965 --> 00:02:20.429
reopen the resume, and identify the target role,

00:02:20.429 --> 00:02:23.894
your strongest example, and your key skills. If

00:02:23.894 --> 00:02:27.358
those are hard to find, move them higher

00:02:27.358 --> 00:02:30.823
and remove less relevant detail. Ask someone else

00:02:30.823 --> 00:02:34.288
what they remember after a quick scan. Your

00:02:34.288 --> 00:02:37.752
next step is to revise one bullet and

00:02:37.752 --> 00:02:40.351
check that every claim is accurate.
